{"created": "2026-11-21T22:10:07.617236+00:00", "modified": "2026-11-21T22:18:26.737477+00:00", "id": 24429650, "conceptrecid": "24416982", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24429650", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.24416982", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24429650", "metadata": {"title": "Rational Fourier certificates for prime gaps, explicit intervals, and arithmetic progressions", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24429650", "publication_date": "2026-11-21", "description": "<p>Assuming the Riemann hypothesis, the limit superior of consecutive prime gaps normalized by &radic;p_n log p_n is less than 0.834051. Under the generalized Riemann hypothesis, for each fixed &epsilon; &gt; 0 and all sufficiently large x, every reduced class modulo 1 &le; q &le; &radic;x/(log x)^(1+&epsilon;) contains a prime in (x, x + 0.851128 &phi;(q)&radic;x log x]. At coefficient 0.85125 the same classes contain at least 8.165&middot;10^(-5) &radic;x primes in the interval. A separate Fourier witness gives, under the ordinary Riemann hypothesis, a prime in (x, x + 0.85125 &radic;x log x] for every real x &ge; 4. For x &ge; 4&middot;10^18 we give an explicit lower bound for the number of primes in the latter interval using a level-set bound for the exterior primes. Rational dual step functions and primal witnesses enclose each of 1/C\u207a(36/11) and 1/C\u207a(4) in an interval of width less than 0.007.</p>\n<p>Files: prime-gaps-v2.pdf (manuscript). prime-gaps-v2-supplement.zip (LaTeX source, figures, rational witnesses, integer and Arb verifiers, Lean 4 certificates, SHA-256 checksums).</p>\n<p>This preprint has not been peer reviewed. AI tools assisted in exploring the rational test functions, developing the analytic estimates, writing the numerical and formal verifiers, and preparing the manuscript.<br><br></p>\n<div>\n<div>Version 2 corrects the order of the author's surnames (Rafael Blanquer Robles) and cites Hasanalizade&ndash;Shen&ndash;Wong and Bellotti&ndash;Wong next to Trudgian's zero-counting bound, which they show remains valid. No theorem, number, witness, or verifier changes.</div>\n</div>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Blanquer Robles, Rafael", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["Prime gaps", "Arithmetic progressions", "Riemann hypothesis", "Generalized Riemann hypothesis", "Explicit formula", "Fourier optimization", "Interval arithmetic", "MSC2020: 11N05, 11N13, 11M26, 42A38"], "version": "2", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "24416982"}}]}}, "title": "Rational Fourier certificates for prime gaps, explicit intervals, and arithmetic progressions", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24429650", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24429650", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24429650?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24429650", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24429650", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.24429650", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24429650/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24416982", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24416982", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24416982", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.24416982", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24429650/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24429650/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24429650/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24429650/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24429650:prime-gaps-v2.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24429650:prime-gaps-v2.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/recor